/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
|  Project    : CFDME-2025-041  Ocotillo WUI Wildfire, Phase 1               |
|  Case       : Ocotillo desert-fire case setup                              |
|  Client     : Ocotillo Additive Structures                                 |
|  Site       : Sonoran Desert buffelgrass WUI, Avra Valley (west of Tucson) |
|  Geometry   : OAS-WUI-01_revC                                              |
|  Export     : Flattened case dictionary bundle (plain ASCII)               |
|                                                                            |
|  Built from : CFDME-2024-018  Dry Wash Aerospace validated case            |
|               (/Projects/CFDME-2024-018_DryWash_Aero/Case/                 |
|                DWA_highaltitude_case_setup.txt)                            |
|                                                                            |
|  Prepared by: Ananya Deshmukh, Mulshi Simulation Labs                      |
|  Date       : 10/09/2025                                                   |
|                                                                            |
|  Header note:                                                              |
|    Based on a validated setup. The Dry Wash Aerospace high-altitude        |
|    external-aerodynamics case (CFDME-2024-018) was validated against       |
|    wind-tunnel data per DWA_validation_memo.pdf and is used here as        |
|    the parent template. Solver, turbulence, freestream, combustion and    |
|    radiation blocks are carried forward from the parent case. Geometry    |
|    and boundary-patch naming have been swapped to the Ocotillo revC       |
|    site model.                                                             |
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/


================================================================================
SECTION 1  --  SOLVER
================================================================================

  application            rhoSimpleFoam
  formulation            steady-state, pressure-based, compressible
  chemistry              none  (non-reacting)
  energy                 sensibleInternalEnergy
  compressible           yes
  transient              no

  Notes:
    rhoSimpleFoam carried forward from the Dry Wash Aerospace validated
    case. Steady, compressible, non-reacting formulation preserved.
    No reactive scalar transport is compiled into the solve.


================================================================================
SECTION 2  --  TURBULENCE
================================================================================

  simulationType         RAS
  RAS
  {
      RASModel                kOmegaSST
      turbulence              on
      printCoeffs             on
  }

  Wall treatment         standard wall functions on all no-slip surfaces
                         (kqRWallFunction / omegaWallFunction /
                          nutkWallFunction, per OpenFOAM defaults)

  Freestream turbulence  I = 0.5 %, mu_t/mu = 5   (inherited from parent
                         reference conditions of record)


================================================================================
SECTION 3  --  FREESTREAM CONDITIONS
================================================================================

  Reference pressure     p_inf   =  26,500 Pa
  Reference temperature  T_inf   =  223 K
  Reference density      rho_inf =  0.4 kg/m3
  Mach number            M_inf   =  0.25
  Reynolds regime        fully turbulent, wall-function resolved

  Notes:
    Freestream block inherited verbatim from the Dry Wash Aerospace
    parent case. The 0.4 kg/m3 reference density is the anchor value
    of the validated parent regime and has been retained here without
    modification.


================================================================================
SECTION 4  --  COMBUSTION MODEL  (NONE)
================================================================================

  combustionModel        none      // no combustion carried forward from parent
  chemistryModel         none
  reactions              (none)
  fvModels               (none active for chemistry or heat release)

  Notes:
    The parent Dry Wash case was non-reacting. No combustion model,
    no fuel source, no oxidizer transport, and no heat-release term
    are compiled into this case. The parent "no combustion" block is
    carried forward verbatim.


================================================================================
SECTION 5  --  RADIATION MODEL  (NONE)
================================================================================

  radiation              off
  radiationProperties    (dictionary intentionally omitted from constant/)

  Notes:
    The parent case carries no radiation participation. No
    radiationProperties dictionary and no radiative source terms in
    fvOptions are present. The parent "no radiation" block is carried
    forward verbatim. Wall surfaces are treated as adiabatic no-slip
    for the aerodynamics loads of interest.


================================================================================
SECTION 6  --  BOUNDARY CONDITIONS  (WALLS)
================================================================================

  Structure / ground / vegetation patch(es) [renamed to Ocotillo site model]:
      type               wall
      U                  fixedValue    (0 0 0)
      p                  zeroGradient
      T                  zeroGradient        // adiabatic
      k                  kqRWallFunction
      omega              omegaWallFunction
      nut                nutkWallFunction

  All wall surfaces use standard wall functions as declared in Section 2.
  No conjugate heat transfer regions are defined; there are no cavity,
  tie, or multi-region entries in constant/. (Wall-function block carried
  forward from the parent case.)


================================================================================
SECTION 7  --  MESH AND GEOMETRY
================================================================================

  Geometry of record     OAS-WUI-01_revC
  Geometry source        Ocotillo Additive Structures, transmitted with
                         Phase 1 SOW package
  Mesh generator         snappyHexMesh
  Mesh build datetime    2025-10-09 morning
  Background mesh        blockMesh, hex-aligned to site axes
  Boundary patch naming  matched to OAS-WUI-01_revC site model
                         (ground, structure, vegetation, inlet, outlet,
                          lateral, top)

  Notes:
    Geometry and mesh are specific to the Ocotillo site. Site topography,
    the printed-concrete structure envelope, and the buffelgrass fuel bed
    footprint are represented from OAS-WUI-01_revC. Boundary-patch names
    on the Ocotillo mesh replace the airframe/body patch names used in
    the parent case. Mesh topology and refinement regions were rebuilt
    against the revC geometry; they are not carried over from the parent.


================================================================================
SECTION 8  --  fvSchemes
================================================================================

  ddtSchemes
  {
      default            steadyState
  }

  gradSchemes
  {
      default            Gauss linear;
      grad(U)            cellLimited Gauss linear 1;
  }

  divSchemes
  {
      default            none;
      div(phi,U)         bounded Gauss upwind;
      div(phi,e)         bounded Gauss upwind;
      div(phi,k)         bounded Gauss upwind;
      div(phi,omega)     bounded Gauss upwind;
      div(((rho*nuEff)*dev2(T(grad(U)))))   Gauss linear;
  }

  laplacianSchemes
  {
      default            Gauss linear corrected;
  }

  interpolationSchemes
  {
      default            linear;
  }

  snGradSchemes
  {
      default            corrected;
  }

  wallDist
  {
      method             meshWave;
  }

  Note: fvSchemes block carried forward verbatim from the parent case;
  first-order upwind advection is consistent with the steady-state
  RANS discretisation on record.


================================================================================
SECTION 9  --  controlDict  (INHERITED)
================================================================================

  application            rhoSimpleFoam;
  startFrom              latestTime;
  startTime              0;
  stopAt                 endTime;
  endTime                3000;                 // iterations (steady)
  deltaT                 1;                    // iteration counter
  writeControl           timeStep;
  writeInterval          500;
  purgeWrite             3;
  writeFormat            binary;
  writePrecision         8;
  writeCompression       off;
  timeFormat             general;
  timePrecision          6;
  runTimeModifiable      true;
  adjustTimeStep         no;

  Function objects:
      residuals          (U, p, e, k, omega)
      wallShearStress    (structure patch)

  Notes:
    controlDict block inherited from the parent case. The application
    field in the live case/system/controlDict has been edited downstream
    to reflect a fire-oriented solver label; the remainder of the
    controlDict entries (time-stepping mode, endTime in iterations,
    writeControl timeStep, adjustTimeStep no) are those shown here as
    inherited from the parent.


================================================================================
END OF EXPORT
================================================================================

  Prepared by:  Ananya Deshmukh, Mulshi Simulation Labs
  Contact:      adeshmukh@mulshisim.in
  Date:         10/09/2025

  Parent case:  /Projects/CFDME-2024-018_DryWash_Aero/Case/
                DWA_highaltitude_case_setup.txt
  This export:  /Projects/CFDME-2025-041_Ocotillo_WUI/Case/system_archive/
                OAS_case_setup_from_DWA.txt

