// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //
// Closing narrative -- S. Bhatia, Mulshi Simulation Labs, 09-Oct-2025
//
// Summary of attempt 3:
//   Iter 1-400:    smooth residual decay across all fields, roughly three
//                  orders of magnitude on U, four on p; behaviour as
//                  expected for a well-posed steady SIMPLE outer loop.
//   Iter 400-800:  residuals for U-components and p enter a periodic
//                  plateau in the band 3e-4 to 8e-4 (Ux initial residual)
//                  and 2e-5 to 3e-5 (p initial residual). T and Uz probes
//                  at probe 0 (plume centreline, x=1.5, z=8) oscillate at
//                  a matching period of ~1.15 s; ~40 K peak-to-peak on T,
//                  ~2.4 m/s on Uz. Residual controls loosened twice: Ux
//                  from 1e-5 to 1e-4 at iter 500, p from 1e-6 to 1e-5 at
//                  iter 700, and the field-averaged residuals still do
//                  not settle inside the loosened tolerance.
//
// Interpretation:
//   This is convergence stalling. The coupled U-p-h-density loop appears
//   to be trapped in a limit cycle driven by the buoyancy-density feedback
//   in the plume core, and is not converging to a steady fixed point.
//
// Recommendation:
//   1. Reduce U under-relaxation further (0.3 -> 0.2) and retry.
//   2. Alternately tighten pressure absolute tolerance to 1e-8 with more
//      GAMG smoother sweeps; the plateau may be numerical noise from the
//      pressure solve rather than a physical mode.
//   3. If neither route breaks the plateau, loosen the outer residual
//      controls one more step (Ux to 1e-3, p to 1e-4) and accept the
//      cycle-averaged field as the initial condition for downstream work.
//
